      en: "Damagaram Takaya is a town in the Zinder Region of southern Niger. It is the administrative center of the Damagaram Takaya Department. The town is located in a rural, agricultural area. The economy is based on subsistence farming, with the main crops being millet and sorghum, and on livestock herding. The population is predominantly Hausa. The town has a local market for the exchange of goods. The department is named after the historical Sultanate of Damagaram (based in Zinder) and the Takaya area. The department was created in 2011."
